 ("h2", "1. Consumers in the Marketplace"),
 ("p", "We participate in the market as producers and as consumers. Consumers buy the final goods and services they need. Earlier chapters showed why rules and regulations are needed: to protect workers in the unorganised sector, to protect borrowers from high interest rates charged by moneylenders and to protect the environment. For example, moneylenders adopt tricks like making a producer sell the produce cheaply or forcing a small farmer such as Swapna to sell her land. Similarly rules are required to protect consumers."),
