 ("p", "In India the consumer movement as a social force originated with the need to protect and promote the interests of consumers against unethical and unfair trade practices. Food shortages, hoarding, black marketing and adulteration of food and edible oil gave birth to the movement in an organised form in the **1960s**. Until the 1970s consumer organisations wrote articles and held exhibitions, and formed groups to look into malpractices in ration shops and overcrowding in road passenger transport. Later the number of consumer groups rose."),
